# ===============================================
# NAVIG core — Git Ignore Configuration
# ===============================================
#
# LAW: `#` starts a comment ONLY at the beginning of a line.
#
# A rule written as `.env    # secrets` is NOT the pattern `.env` — git matches the
# whole literal string, spaces and "# secrets" included, so the rule silently
# matches nothing. This file previously carried 80 such rules: `.env`, `.env.*`,
# `*.pem`, `.coverage`, `.mypy_cache/` and `.pytest_cache/` were ALL dead, which is
# how a 53 KB `.coverage` database ended up committed. Put every explanation on its
# OWN line above the pattern it explains. Never append one after a pattern.
#
# Locally generated artifacts belong under `.dev/` — see pyproject.toml
# ([tool.ruff] cache-dir, [tool.mypy] cache_dir, [tool.coverage.run] data_file)
# and pytest.ini (cache_dir, --basetemp).

# ===============================================
# Python
# ===============================================
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.pyd
.Python

# Build / packaging output
build/
dist/
sdist/
develop-eggs/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
wheels/
parts/
var/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST
cython_debug/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# ===============================================
# Development artifacts — everything generated locally lives under .dev/
# ===============================================
# The bare cache patterns below are a safety net for a tool run with an explicit
# config override, or for a checkout predating the .dev/ redirect.
.dev/
.local/
.archive/
.backup/
.backups/

.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pytype/
.pyre/
.pytest_cache/
.benchmarks/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/

.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.cover

# pytest --basetemp dirs (all historical variants)
.pytest_tmp/
.pytest_tmp*/
pytest_tmp*/
*.pytest_tmp/

# ===============================================
# Secrets and credentials — NEVER commit
# ===============================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.token
secrets.yaml
credentials.json
config/secrets.*
*_credentials.*
discord-webhooks.json
discord-*.json

# NAVIG vault: AES-256 encrypted blobs + key material
*.enc
.blackbox/
**/.blackbox/
vault.salt

# Ed25519 private keys for license signing / founder key material.
tools/license_keys/

# Local Cloudflare token sandbox
cf.txt

# ===============================================
# Databases, logs, process state
# ===============================================
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.log
*.pid
logs/
nohup.out

# ===============================================
# Editors and OS
# ===============================================
# `.vscode/*` (not `.vscode/`) so the shared settings file can be re-included —
# git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
Thumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.directory
.Trash-*
*.lnk
nul
$null

# Merge / edit leftovers
*.orig
*.bak
*.backup

# ===============================================
# Node (tooling only; core itself is pure Python)
# ===============================================
node_modules/

# ===============================================
# AI IDE configuration — per-developer overrides only
# ===============================================
.augment
.clinerules
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.agent/
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/

# ===============================================
# NAVIG runtime state
# ===============================================
# ~/.navig/ is the global user store and never belongs in a repo. The project
# `.navig/` directory is runtime state here in core and is ignored wholesale.
.navig/
.navig_worktrees/
userdata/
temp_restore/

# Private dev-only plugin
navig/plugins/llm_bridge/
navig/plugins/llm-bridge/

# Bot stack (separate private repo)
navig_ai.py
navig_bot.py
run_navig.py
navig_harness.py
requirements-bot.txt

# Private local docs
knowledge/
.github/instructions/local-developer.instructions.md

# Experimental reference corpus (never shipped)
.lab/

# Community mirror lives at the monorepo root under registry/
navig-community/

# icons/ moved to .navig/brand/; ignore any root-level recreation
icons/

# NOTE: `latest.json` is deliberately NOT ignored. The old rule called it a "stale
# release metadata artifact", but core/latest.json is the CANONICAL release manifest:
# scripts/_version_sync.py writes it (config/latest.json is the mirror) and
# .github/workflows/ci.yml guards its version against pyproject.toml. The rule was
# dead (trailing `# comment`), which is the only reason it never broke a release.

# host/ build output — the tracked manifests stay, binaries and logs do not
host/out.log
host/build_errors.txt
host/*.exe
host/crates/**/target/
**/target/

# ===============================================
# navig-os workspace scaffold (runtime state — NEVER commit)
# ===============================================
# When navig-os (apps/os) manages a directory as a "workspace" it scaffolds this
# exact set of files/dirs at the workspace root. Pointing navig-os at core/ — which
# is the Python package, NOT a workspace — littered these here as untracked files
# that cluttered every `git status`. The monorepo root ignores the same set; these
# rules are the core/-scoped mirror. None of these names is a legitimate core file:
# core's real config is pyproject.toml.
/config.json
/events.jsonl
/install.json
/views.json
/labels/
/statuses/
/sources/
/sessions/
/skills/
# core/workflows/ is NOT a core directory either: the automation engine loads from
# config_dir()/workflows (navig/core/automation_engine.py), never from the repo.
/workflows/
/.claude-plugin/
/.inbox
/.agents
/plans/
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md

# ===============================================
# Historical note — do NOT re-add a bare `store/` rule
# ===============================================
# A bare `store/` used to sit here to keep "runtime store" content out of VCS, but
# the runtime store lives in ~/.navig/data/store (platform.paths.store_dir), never
# in the repo. All the rule ever did was SILENTLY swallow tracked content:
#   * `navig/store/` (BaseStore source code) had to be rescued with a !negation;
#   * 13 authored builtin blocks were dropped by `git add` and never shipped.
# The built-in content store is now navig/builtin/ (tracked, shipped in the wheel
# via package-data).
navig/store/**/__pycache__/

# uv.lock is NOT this repo's lockfile. requirements.lock is canonical (SECURITY.md,
# docs/dev/development.md: "do not add a separate uv.lock for this repo"). One was
# committed by accident inside a bulk commit, went stale at navig 2.9.1 while the project
# reached 3.25.0, was shipped in nothing and read by nothing -- and was the sole source of
# all 8 Dependabot alerts on the public repo. Ignored so it cannot come back silently the
# next time someone runs `uv lock`.
uv.lock
